    "turn_idx": 43,
    "turn_text": "So right now homelessness is governed by a law called Lanterman Petrus Short passed in 1967. LPS. LPS has as a standard that you cannot take someone into custodial care. if they are not an imminent threat to themselves or others. That standard is too high. It means that people who are drug addicted or mentally ill who cannot function independently are being left on the street with no assistance. We need to change the standard. We need to change it to someone who's drug addicted or mentally ill who cannot conduct their affairs for themselves. We change the law. Okay, so that's what governance is about. You change the law and then you implement the law. We lower the standard, we get these people, the medical treatment they need for their drug addiction, the counseling for their mental illness. We help them get back to being functioning, contributing citizens. And where do we get the funding for all the mental health and everything",
